cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below. narrative-audit is
  a fork of abstract-audit (Ajay Mandyam Rangarajan); if you use the
  inherited pipeline, metrics or judge protocol, please also cite the
  abstract-audit software and its paper (references below).
type: software
title: narrative-audit
authors:
  - family-names: Pazooki
    given-names: Hossain
repository-code: https://github.com/hossainpazooki/narrative-audit
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A measurement pipeline testing whether narrative quality, as
  operationalized from Neel Nanda's "Highly Opinionated Advice on How
  to Write ML Papers", predicts age-normalized citations among accepted
  NeurIPS papers (1987-2025). Built on the abstract-audit pipeline.
references:
  - type: software
    title: abstract-audit
    authors:
      - family-names: Mandyam Rangarajan
        given-names: Ajay
    repository-code: https://github.com/armandyam/abstract-audit
    license: MIT
    notes: >-
      The base pipeline this repository forks: stage runner, schema,
      classical writing metrics, LLM-judge protocol, reference outputs
      and verification. Derived data (judge_scores/, reference/) is
      CC BY 4.0, see LICENSE-DATA.
  - type: conference-paper
    title: >-
      LLM Judges Agree With Each Other and Disagree With Human-Grounded
      Readability Metrics
    authors:
      - family-names: Mandyam Rangarajan
        given-names: Ajay
      - family-names: Krishnan
        given-names: Jeyashree
    year: 2026
    conference:
      name: The Third Workshop on Uncertainty-Aware NLP
    url: https://openreview.net/forum?id=sOKzkunyhD
  - type: conference-paper
    title: Measurable Writing Standards for AI-Native Venues
    authors:
      - family-names: Mandyam Rangarajan
        given-names: Ajay
      - family-names: Krishnan
        given-names: Jeyashree
    year: 2026
    conference:
      name: >-
        NeurIPS 2026 Workshop on AI-Native Academia: Authorship, Peer
        Review, and Conference Governance under AI
    url: https://openreview.net/forum?id=JXxRLziwgY
